      "text": "The given polynomial has roots \\(3\\) and \\(-2\\). Let the third root be \\(r\\). Therefore, the polynomial can be expressed as:\n\\[\na(x-3)(x+2)(x-r)\n\\]\nFirst, we expand the polynomial \\((x-3)(x+2)\\):\n\\[\n(x-3)(x+2) = x^2 + 2x - 3x - 6 = x^2 - x - 6\n\\]\nNext, we multiply this result by \\((x-r)\\):\n\\[\n(x^2 - x - 6)(x - r) = x^3 - rx^2 - x^2 + rx - 6x + 6r = x^3 - (r+1)x^2 + (r-6)x + 6r\n\\]\nThus, the polynomial is:\n\\[\na(x^3 - (r+1)x^2 + (r-6)x + 6r)\n\\]\nBy comparing coefficients with the general form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), we identify:\n\\[\nb = -a(r+1), \\quad c = a(r-6), \\quad d = 6ar\n\\]\nWe need to find \\(\\frac{b+c}{a}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{b+c}{a} = \\frac{-a(r+1) + a(r-6)}{a} = \\frac{-ar - a + ar - 6a}{a} = \\frac{-a - 6a}{a} = \\frac{-7a}{a} = -7\n\\]\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-7}\n\\]",
